@startsalt
' Screen: Dataset Entry Add/Edit Form
' User Stories:
'   - US-411: As a developer, I can manually add or edit a dataset entry
'   - US-412: As a developer, I can toggle between plain text and JSON input mode
'   - US-413: As a developer, I can tag entries for filtering and breakdown reporting

{
  <b>CodeFre.sh</b> | Evaluation | Datasets | Customer Support QA | <b>Edit Entry: cs_001_refund</b>
  ==
  {
    <b>Edit Entry</b>
    <i>Dataset: Customer Support QA · Type: request_response</i>
    ==
    <b>Entry Key</b> <i>(required, unique within dataset)</i>
    "cs_001_refund                                                       "
    --
    <b>Input</b> <i>(required)</i>
    {
      [Plain Text] | [JSON ▾] | <i>Format: plain text</i>
    }
    {+
      "My order hasn't arrived and it's been 2 weeks since I placed it.  "
      "Order #ORD-88214. I paid for express shipping. I want a refund.   "
      "                                                                    "
    }
    --
    <b>Expected Output</b> <i>(required)</i>
    {
      [Plain Text] | [JSON ▾] | <i>Format: plain text</i>
    }
    {+
      "I understand your frustration. Let me look up your order #ORD-88214"
      "right away. Based on your express shipping, this should have arrived"
      "within 2-3 business days. I'll process a full refund immediately.  "
    }
    --
    <b>Tags</b>
    "billing ×" | "refund ×" | "shipping ×" | "add tag..." |
    <i>Press Enter or comma to add. Tags used for breakdown reports and filtering.</i>
    --
    <b>Notes</b> <i>(optional, internal only)</i>
    {+
      "Edge case: customer explicitly mentions express shipping — agent    "
      "should acknowledge SLA breach proactively.                         "
    }
    ==
    {
      [Cancel] | [Save Entry]
    }
  }
}
@endsalt
